course: dictionary
lesson: 4436
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning the writer wants. Those surrounding words are the context. «Handle» is a good example: it can be a thing you hold, an action, or a way of coping.
explain: «Turn the pan handle inward on the stove so no one knocks it.» You can turn a handle and knock it, so here a handle is the part you hold. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: «I can handle it» means I can cope with it. The words «I can» are the clue. Here handle is a verb, which means to deal with or manage something. Same word, different job, and the sentence shows you which one.
fact: A handle is the part of a door, cup, pan, bag or tool that you hold.
fact: To handle something means to touch it or hold it in your hands.
fact: To handle a problem or situation means to deal with it or manage it.
fact: «Fly off the handle» means suddenly get very angry.
fact: «Get a handle on» means understand.
exercise: «Use child scissors, carry them closed and pointing down, and pass them handle first.» What is the handle on scissors? | *The part you hold | The box they came in | The sharp blade | The screw in the middle
exercise: «I can handle it» means what? | *I can cope with it | I can name it | I can pick it up | I can break it
exercise: Look at the box label «handle with care». What does handle mean here? | The box is empty | Please open the box now | It is very heavy | *Fragile, so treat it gently
test: «He would fly off the handle if the bus was late.» What does «fly off the handle» mean? | Become very calm | *Suddenly get very angry | Lose the handle of a bag | Fly through the air
test: «Vets use sleep medicine only when an animal cannot be handled safely.» What does handled mean here? | Named online | Cooked in a pan | *Touched, held or managed safely | Closed in a box
exam: «Wash your hands after you handle the animals and equipment.» What does handle mean in this sentence? | A name you use online | A part you grip on a door | To deal with a problem | *To touch or hold something
